R = {
 "Dark Gift of Drizlash, the Nine-Eyed Spider|COS": {"d": "You can walk on walls and hang upside down from ceilings, and you need no ability check to climb even the hardest surfaces. An extra eye grows somewhere on your body. It cannot see and it never closes."},
 "Dark Gift of Fekre, Queen of Poxes|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can cast Contagion. After the third cast, the gift is gone. Your body gives off a foul stench of filth.", "ch": [3, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Contagion", 0]]},
 "Dark Gift of Great Taar Haak, the Five-Headed Destroyer|COS": {"d": "You gain the strength of a Belt of Fire Giant Strength for 10 days, then the gift is gone. You also take on this flaw: \"I like to bully others and make them feel weak and inferior.\""},
 "Dark Gift of Khirad, the Star of Secrets|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can cast Scrying. After the third cast, the gift is gone. Your voice sinks to a low whisper and your smile turns cruel and wicked.", "ch": [3, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Scrying", 0]]},
 "Dark Gift of Norganas, the Finger of Oblivion|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can cast Finger of Death. After the third cast, the gift is gone. When it goes, you must succeed on a DC 15 Constitution saving throw or drop to 0 Hit Points. Your blood turns black and thick like tar.", "ch": [3, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Finger of Death", 0]]},
 "Dark Gift of Savnok the Inscrutable|COS": {"d": "You are under a Mind Blank spell whose duration is stretched to 1 year, after which the gift is gone. Your eyes melt away and leave empty sockets, yet you can still see."},
 "Dark Gift of Seriach, the Hell Hound Whisperer|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can summon and control two Hell Hounds, which appear together. You can do this only once, and the gift is gone when the hounds die. You learn to speak and understand Infernal if you do not know it already. The hounds understand no other language. Sulfurous smoke seeps from your pores whenever you speak Infernal.", "ch": [1, "0", "never"]},
 "Dark Gift of Shami-Amourae, the Lady of Delights|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can cast Suggestion, and saving throws against it have Disadvantage. After the third cast, the gift is gone. You grow an extra finger on each hand and take on this flaw: \"I can't get enough pleasure. I desire others to create beauty for me at all times.\"", "ch": [3, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Suggestion", 0]]},
 "Dark Gift of Sykane, the Soul Hungerer|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can cast Raise Dead. After the third cast, the gift is gone. Your eyes glow a sickly yellow until then. You also take on this flaw: \"If I help someone, I expect payment in return.\"", "ch": [3, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Raise Dead", 0]]},
 "Dark Gift of Tarakamedes, the Grave Wyrm|COS": {"d": "Skeletal wings sprout from your back and give you a Fly Speed of 50 feet. You must eat bones or grave dirt to live. At dawn, if you have not eaten at least 1 pound of them in the past 24 hours, you die.", "fx": {"fly": 50}},
 "Dark Gift of Vaund the Evasive|COS": {"d": "You gain the benefits of an Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location and a Ring of Evasion for 10 days, then the gift is gone. You become twitchy and nervous and take on this flaw: \"I can't give a straight answer to any question put to me.\""},
 "Dark Gift of Yog the Invincible|COS": {"d": "Your Hit Point maximum rises by 30 for 10 days, then the gift is gone. Oily black fur covers your face and body."},
 "Dark Gift of Yrrga, the Eye of Shadows|COS": {"d": "You have Truesight out to 60 feet for 30 days, then the gift is gone. Your eyes become starry voids until then. You also take on this flaw: \"I believe that all life is pointless and look forward to death when it finally comes.\""},
 "Dark Gift of Zantras, the Kingmaker|COS": {"d": "Your Charisma score rises by 4, up to a maximum of 22. You take on this flaw: \"I won't take no for an answer.\"", "fx": {"abil": ["CHA", 4, 22]}},
 "Dark Gift of Zrin-Hala, the Howling Storm|COS": {"d": "As an action, you can cast Lightning Bolt. After the third cast, the gift is gone. One side of your face sags and loses all feeling.", "ch": [3, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Lightning Bolt", 0]]},
 "Dimir Charm|GGR": {"d": "When you activate this charm, you can cast Blink or Sleep (as a 3rd-level spell). Or, when you take damage, you can use your Reaction to turn Invisible and teleport up to 30 feet to an unoccupied space you can see. You stay Invisible until the start of your next turn or until you attack or cast a spell. The charm is gone after you activate it.", "ch": [1, "0", "never"], "sp": [["Blink", 0], ["Sleep", 0]]},
 "Draconic Familiar|FTD": {"d": "A draconic familiar aids you, perhaps a sliver of the mind of the dragon who empowered you. You can cast Find Familiar as a ritual with no material components. Cast this way, the familiar always takes the form of a Pseudodragon. Also, when you take the Attack action, you can give up one of your attacks so your Pseudodragon familiar can make one attack with its Reaction.", "sp": [["Find Familiar", 0]]},
 "Draconic Rebirth|FTD": {"d": "You become a dragonborn. Your original race's traits are replaced by those of a chromatic, gem, or metallic dragonborn, matching the family of the dragon behind this gift. You may keep the skill proficiencies from your old race, or gain proficiency in two skills of your choice."},
 "Draconic Senses|FTD": {"d": "You gain a dragon's keen senses. You have Blindsight out to 10 feet. In that range you can see anything not behind cover, even if you are Blinded or in darkness, and you can see Invisible creatures unless they hide successfully. You also have Advantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks.", "fx": {"adv": ["Perception"]}},
 "Dragon Queen's Will|DSOTDQ": {"d": "You glimpse the ambitions of the Dragon Queen. Her vision haunts your dreams but hardens your will against her. You gain a +4 bonus to Wisdom saving throws. After three uses, the charm is gone. Until then you have harmless but unsettling dreams of ravenous dragons. You also permanently learn Draconic if you did not know it.", "ch": [3, "0", "never"]},
 "Echo of Dragonsight|FTD": {"d": "Your awareness reaches past the single world you call home. You can cast Contact Other Plane as a ritual. The being you reach is a dragon on another world of the Material Plane, so what it knows of your world may be limited. It is also an echo of the dragon behind this gift, which can color its attitude and behavior toward you.", "sp": [["Contact Other Plane", 0]]},
 "Ephara's Devotee|MOT": {"d": "Requires Piety 3 or higher with Ephara. Ephara gives you insight into how people communicate. You can cast Comprehend Languages with no material component a number of times equal to your Intelligence modifier (minimum once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for it.", "sp": [["Comprehend Languages", 0]]},
 "Ephara's Disciple|MOT": {"d": "Requires Piety 25 or higher with Ephara. You can cast Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum with no material components. Once you cast it this way, you cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest. Intelligence is your spellcasting ability for it.", "ch": [1, "long", "long"], "sp": [["Mordenkainen's Private Sanctum", 0]]},
 "Ephara's Votary|MOT": {"d": "Requires Piety 10 or higher with Ephara. You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks while in a city. Also, when you fail an Intelligence check or Intelligence saving throw, you can reroll the die and must use the new roll. After using this reroll, you cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest.", "ch": [1, "long", "long"]},
 "Erebos's Devotee|MOT": {"d": "Requires Piety 3 or higher with Erebos. You have proven yourself an enforcer of the grim laws of the Underworld. You can call on Erebos's favor to cast Bane with no material components a number of times equal to your Wisdom modifier (minimum once). You regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.", "sp": [["Bane", 0]]},
 "Erebos's Disciple|MOT": {"d": "Requires Piety 25 or higher with Erebos. When a soul is sent to its rightful place, you can draw on the energy of the Underworld. When a creature dies within 10 feet of you, you can use your Reaction to gain Temporary Hit Points equal to your level."},
 "Erebos's Votary|MOT": {"d": "Requires Piety 10 or higher with Erebos. You can cast Vampiric Touch. Once you cast it this way, you cannot do so again until you finish a Long Rest. Wisdom is your spellcasting ability for it.", "ch": [1, "long", "long"], "sp": [["Vampiric Touch", 0]]},
 "Eyes of the Impossible|TOFW": {"d": "Knowledge you should never have scars you. Your eyes turn black except for white pupils. You have Advantage on Charisma (Persuasion) checks made to deal with evil creatures. You can also cast Eyebite as an action. Your spellcasting ability for it is Intelligence, Wisdom, or Charisma, chosen when you gain this charm. After you cast it, you cannot cast it again until the next dawn. The charm is gone after 13 days, when your looks return to normal.", "ch": [1, "0", "dawn"], "sp": [["Eyebite", 0]]},
 "Favor of the Heroic Steed|DSOTDQ": {"d": "Two heroic steeds judge you worthy and agree to serve you. This charm has 2 charges. As an action, you can spend 1 charge to summon a Warhorse wearing plate barding (AC 18). The warhorse serves you for 24 hours, then vanishes.", "ch": [2, "0", "never"]},
 "Final Breath|VRGR": {"d": "A deity's favored servant lies dying and calls down divine wrath. Pronouncement: the dying creature tells the killer, \"May your mind grow dim in battle until the sun sets forever.\" Burden: the character has Disadvantage on attack rolls because of short, random bouts of confusion. Resolution: to lift the curse, the character must bring about a symbolic setting of the sun or a strengthening of the night to appease the slain creature's deity. Examples are stopping a festival for a sun god, or performing a ritual that wraps a whole settlement in magical night for 24 hours."},
}
